# project: payments-reconciliation-hardening
VAR runs = 0
VAR clean_streak = 0

-> rework_matching_engine

=== rework_matching_engine ===
Rework the matching engine for the payments reconciliation job.
Done means the redesigned engine is deployed to the nightly job and ready for a fresh set of retry runs.
~ runs = 0
~ clean_streak = 0
+ [Engine reworked, start the retry runs] -> run_reconciliation

=== run_reconciliation ===
Run the nightly reconciliation with the reworked engine; at most five runs per rework cycle.
~ runs += 1
+ [Run reconciled clean] -> record_clean
+ [Run had breaks] -> record_dirty
+ [QA pulls the plug, back to the drawing board] @human ~loop~ -> rework_matching_engine

=== record_clean ===
Record a clean run; two clean runs in a row end the retries early.
~ clean_streak += 1
+ {clean_streak >= 2} [Two clean in a row, call it done early] -> finance_review
+ {clean_streak < 2 && runs < 5} [Streak not proven yet, run again] ~loop~ -> run_reconciliation
+ {clean_streak < 2 && runs >= 5} [Five runs used up] -> finance_review

=== record_dirty ===
Record a run with breaks; the clean streak resets.
~ clean_streak = 0
+ {runs < 5} [Retry the nightly reconciliation] ~loop~ -> run_reconciliation
+ {runs >= 5} [Five runs used up] -> finance_review

=== finance_review ===
Finance reviews the final match rate, whether retries ended early, ran out, or QA never intervened.
* [Match rate above 99.9 percent, sign off] @human -> END
* [Match rate not above 99.9 percent, escalate] @human -> cfo_escalation

=== cfo_escalation ===
CFO decides how to close the match-rate shortfall.
* [Buy a vendor product] @human -> adopt_vendor_product
* [Keep the manual process] @human -> keep_manual_process

=== adopt_vendor_product ===
Procure and roll out the vendor reconciliation product to replace the in-house matcher.
-> END

=== keep_manual_process ===
Keep the manual reconciliation process in place alongside the existing job.
-> END
